Dear Security Team,

Your team has been identified through public CTF rankings (CTFtime) as a potential qualifier for DEF CON 31 CTF (Las Vegas, August 2027). Team registration for the online qualifiers is now open.

Qualifier Details:
  Format: Jeopardy + Attack-Defense (48 hours)
  Dates: March 15-17, 2027 (Fri 18:00 UTC - Sun 18:00 UTC)
  Team Size: 2-6 members
  Qualification Slots: Top 16 teams advance to DEF CON finals
  Categories: Pwn / Web / Rev / Crypto / Misc / Sandbox Escape

Team Registration:
Registration is done through the CTFtime platform. Please navigate to qualifier.ctftime.org in your browser and log in with your existing CTFtime account. Do NOT use any registration links from email — always access CTFtime directly.

Practice Challenges:
Three warm-up challenges are live on the platform:
  "quarantine": Escaping a seccomp-sandboxed SMTP parser
  "homograph": Find the punycode in a chain of lookalike domains
  "ghost_pixel": Extract a message from a CSS tracking pixel

Security note:
DEF CON and CTFtime will NEVER ask you to:
  - Complete OAuth authorization through an email link
  - Grant "offline_access" or any token scope via email
  - Register on a non-CTFtime.org domain
If you receive such an email claiming to be from DEF CON, it is a phishing attempt targeting security researchers. Please report it to the DEF CON security team (security@defcon.example).

See you in Vegas.

DEF CON 31 CTF Organizing Committee
